1
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:29,390
[Live Forever]

2
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:32,890
[Episode 4]

3
00:01:09,950 --> 00:01:11,280
What are you doing here?

4
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:13,340
Where is your curator?

5
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:14,640
Curator Lin isn't here.

6
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:15,300
He went out.

7
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,410
You're new here?

8
00:01:16,690 --> 00:01:18,360
Director Song comes here every month.

9
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:18,960
After you.

10
00:01:20,840 --> 00:01:21,510
You can't go in.

11
00:01:21,510 --> 00:01:22,560
Do you have an appointment?

12
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,690
You can't enter without appointment.

13
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:31,590
That batch of Ming Dynasty paintings

14
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:34,640
needs to be sent to the provincial office
for approval by 8 tomorrow.

15
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:36,400
If we don't finish reviewing them today,

16
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:38,420
and the higher-ups hold us accountable,

17
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:39,680
are you going to take the blame,

18
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,729
or am I?

19
00:01:41,759 --> 00:01:42,570
Ning,

20
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:43,950
how did you communicate with them?

21
00:01:43,950 --> 00:01:45,150
I'm sorry, Director.

22
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:48,229
So inefficient.

23
00:01:49,910 --> 00:01:51,960
We've already called Curator Lin.

24
00:01:52,560 --> 00:01:53,610
[ID Badge]

25
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:54,770
You're Zhao, right?

26
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:56,729
He said you should show us right in.

27
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Oh, you've called him?

28
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,310
Look, I didn't know.

29
00:02:01,030 --> 00:02:01,670
Go on in.

30
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:02,520
I'm not going.

31
00:02:02,520 --> 00:02:04,030
I'm not going, okay?

32
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,639
Business first. Let's go.

33
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:10,479
How could I let you carry my bag?

34
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:12,140
What would that look like?

35
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:13,550
You carry it.

36
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:15,390
- Right this way.
- Yes, Director.

37
00:02:15,390 --> 00:02:16,250
Take your time.

38
00:02:18,990 --> 00:02:20,640
Awesome!

39
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,240
I didn't know you could do this.

40
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:23,770
You're not so bad yourself.

41
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:02,990
You just won't leave me alone, will you?

42
00:03:09,590 --> 00:03:10,480
A good dog doesn't block the way.

43
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,430
I've searched everywhere inside.

44
00:03:11,430 --> 00:03:12,200
Nothing is there.

45
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,360
Let's just go home.

46
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:13,890
Let's go.

47
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,150
Let's go.

48
00:03:15,150 --> 00:03:18,010
- What if someone sees us later?
- What are you doing?

49
00:03:46,710 --> 00:03:53,920
Newspapers! Newspapers!

50
00:03:56,150 --> 00:03:57,280
Excuse me, make way.

51
00:03:57,550 --> 00:03:59,079
Excuse me, coming through.

52
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:08,870
Excuse me, make way.

53
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,470
Save the nation.

54
00:04:51,590 --> 00:04:52,880
Restore our homeland.

55
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:55,170
This is a time of critical peril.

56
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:58,710
May our compatriots awaken together.

57
00:05:02,150 --> 00:05:03,760
If our homeland falls,

58
00:05:03,830 --> 00:05:05,830
who can remain unscathed?

59
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,440
Since we were born in this era,

60
00:05:08,910 --> 00:05:10,590
we must do something.

61
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:11,790
Commander,

62
00:05:12,710 --> 00:05:14,370
we've brought Miss Song back.

63
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:33,610
You're back.

64
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:36,800
Didn't you send people
to follow me

65
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:39,440
and bring me back with such fanfare?

66
00:05:39,990 --> 00:05:42,390
Now you're acting like you don't remember?

67
00:05:49,210 --> 00:05:51,070
It's not safe outside these days.

68
00:05:51,350 --> 00:05:53,010
The students are protesting.

69
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,610
It's safer to stay at home.

70
00:05:55,710 --> 00:05:56,960
But the newspaper office hasn't

71
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:59,620
sent anyone
to pick up the drafts for a long time.

72
00:06:00,830 --> 00:06:03,360
If I don't deliver them now,
it'll be too late.

73
00:06:04,110 --> 00:06:05,650
The person from the newspaper office

74
00:06:05,650 --> 00:06:07,780
who delivered your drafts was killed.

75
00:06:10,030 --> 00:06:11,880
The content of your newspaper
has angered certain people.

76
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:14,280
If this continues,
you'll be in danger too.

77
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:17,070
Killed?

78
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:22,000
He was only nineteen.

79
00:06:24,470 --> 00:06:25,560
Who couldn't tolerate

80
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,200
a nineteen-year-old kid?

81
00:06:27,790 --> 00:06:28,960
Was it the police,

82
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:30,180
the Green Gang,

83
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:33,750
or you people in high positions?

84
00:06:38,250 --> 00:06:38,890
Qiu...

85
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:39,620
Commander,

86
00:06:39,659 --> 00:06:40,920
there's an emergency.

87
00:06:48,140 --> 00:06:49,210
I'll be back later.

88
00:07:05,390 --> 00:07:07,510
I must send these drawings out.

89
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:12,090
I will deliver them myself.

90
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:15,620
[Song Baiwei]

91
00:07:16,150 --> 00:07:16,960
Commander,

92
00:07:16,980 --> 00:07:18,460
the situation
is deteriorating again.

93
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:20,660
The higher-ups say we must take action.

94
00:07:22,190 --> 00:07:23,000
Find someone

95
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,230
to specifically help Miss Song

96
00:07:25,230 --> 00:07:27,010
deliver her drawings
to the newspaper from now on.

97
00:07:27,010 --> 00:07:27,560
Yes, sir.

98
00:07:32,270 --> 00:07:33,650
Save the nation!

99
00:07:33,830 --> 00:07:35,620
Save the nation!

100
00:07:35,650 --> 00:07:37,260
Revitalize China!

101
00:07:37,320 --> 00:07:38,960
Revitalize China!

102
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,560
Strengthen ourselves to save the country!

103
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,270
Strengthen ourselves to save the country!

104
00:07:42,270 --> 00:07:43,830
Revitalize China!

105
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:45,470
Revitalize China!

106
00:07:45,470 --> 00:07:47,080
Strengthen ourselves to save the country!

107
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:49,230
Strengthen ourselves to save the country!

108
00:07:49,230 --> 00:07:50,710
Save the nation!

109
00:07:50,710 --> 00:07:52,270
Save the nation!

110
00:07:52,270 --> 00:07:53,610
-Fall back!
-Strengthen ourselves to save the country!

111
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:55,440
-Fall back!
-Strengthen ourselves to save the country!

112
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,710
Revitalize China!

113
00:07:56,730 --> 00:07:58,120
Revitalize China!

114
00:07:58,330 --> 00:07:59,650
Fall back, hurry!

115
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:01,120
Fall back! What are you doing?

116
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,180
What are you doing?

117
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:03,880
Trying to rebel?

118
00:08:03,910 --> 00:08:05,320
Why are you arresting us?

119
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,380
You damn traitors!

120
00:08:19,410 --> 00:08:20,290
Go back!

121
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,230
Get in!

122
00:08:22,730 --> 00:08:23,530
Little girl,

123
00:08:23,700 --> 00:08:26,030
go home quickly. It's too dangerous here.

124
00:08:27,150 --> 00:08:28,680
What are you talking about?

125
00:08:48,090 --> 00:08:48,890
Follow me.

126
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:05,620
Search over there.

127
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:07,040
Hurry!

128
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:19,630
It should be safe now.

129
00:09:20,250 --> 00:09:22,190
I'm not very familiar with this area.

130
00:09:22,190 --> 00:09:23,420
But why didn't you...

131
00:09:53,090 --> 00:09:54,050
Doesn't it hurt?

132
00:09:57,630 --> 00:09:58,400
I...

133
00:10:00,270 --> 00:10:01,310
I'm sorry.

134
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:05,500
I thought you were a member
of our student association,

135
00:10:05,530 --> 00:10:07,270
being chased by those bad guys too.

136
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:08,800
You're from the student association?

137
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:09,590
Yes.

138
00:10:10,470 --> 00:10:11,960
I'm Lin Huai, the president

139
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,740
of the National Salvation
Student Association,

140
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:14,380
Have we...

141
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:17,080
met somewhere before?

142
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:18,630
Hey,

143
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:20,830
your way of hitting on girls

144
00:10:20,830 --> 00:10:22,090
is too old-fashioned.

145
00:10:22,750 --> 00:10:23,440
I'm serious, I...

146
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:25,680
Instead of spending time hitting on girls,

147
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:27,880
you'd better bandage your wound first.

148
00:10:32,830 --> 00:10:33,510
Here.

149
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:48,350
Let me do it.

150
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:54,900
Your hand.

151
00:11:01,470 --> 00:11:02,280
Turn it over.

152
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:12,750
Thank you.

153
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:14,630
Do you know how many people

154
00:11:14,630 --> 00:11:17,040
have a problem
with your student association?

155
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:18,660
And you're still shouting that

156
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:19,490
you're the president.

157
00:11:19,490 --> 00:11:20,610
Do you have a death wish?

158
00:11:20,610 --> 00:11:22,890
I really feel like we've met before.

159
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:26,210
Okay, okay.

160
00:11:27,350 --> 00:11:28,140
We've met.

161
00:11:28,810 --> 00:11:30,190
We met thousands of years ago.

162
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:31,520
Are you satisfied now?

163
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:34,420
Thanks for helping me today.

164
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,440
But it's not safe outside right now.

165
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:38,240
You should hurry back to school.

166
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:51,870
There's a sniper!

167
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:52,830
Go!

168
00:12:19,990 --> 00:12:21,390
Don't poke your head out.

169
00:12:21,810 --> 00:12:23,440
They'll come after you again
since they failed.

170
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:24,320
Run!

171
00:12:24,990 --> 00:12:25,940
Run!

172
00:12:25,990 --> 00:12:26,640
No.

173
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:27,590
I'm not leaving.

174
00:12:28,830 --> 00:12:29,920
We leave together.

175
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:32,100
I'll take you to the hospital.

176
00:12:32,730 --> 00:12:34,010
I won't die.

177
00:12:35,230 --> 00:12:36,230
Just go!

178
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:37,830
Go!

179
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:40,140
Go!

180
00:14:12,420 --> 00:14:13,460
Let go!

181
00:15:08,970 --> 00:15:09,730
Are you

182
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,540
here for a tour?

183
00:15:13,510 --> 00:15:15,280
Yes, just passing by.

184
00:15:23,710 --> 00:15:24,590
Have we...

185
00:15:25,350 --> 00:15:27,080
met somewhere before?

186
00:15:33,530 --> 00:15:34,530
My name is Lin Huai.

187
00:15:34,530 --> 00:15:36,460
I'm the curator of this art gallery.

188
00:15:36,460 --> 00:15:37,530
Nice to meet you.

189
00:15:43,350 --> 00:15:45,810
Didn't we just meet yesterday,
Curator Lin?

190
00:15:45,810 --> 00:15:46,500
This is Song Yiqiu,

191
00:15:46,500 --> 00:15:47,270
my wife.

192
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:49,560
Ex-wife.

193
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:49,990
Just divorced.

194
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:50,870
She's a bit emotional.

195
00:15:50,870 --> 00:15:51,870
You know how it is.

196
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:56,410
I understand.

197
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:02,200
Lin Huai.

198
00:16:03,910 --> 00:16:04,700
Curator,

199
00:16:06,650 --> 00:16:08,440
sorry for the abrupt intrusion.

200
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:11,110
We are also enthusiasts
of famous painting research.

201
00:16:11,110 --> 00:16:13,570
We heard your gallery
has a rich collection.

202
00:16:13,750 --> 00:16:14,960
We're very curious.

203
00:16:14,990 --> 00:16:15,750
I wonder

204
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:18,320
if you could give us a tour?

205
00:16:19,290 --> 00:16:20,850
Do you have any collections similar to

206
00:16:20,850 --> 00:16:23,650
Autumn Moon in the Forest?

207
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:25,280
Because we are

208
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,400
especially, you know...

209
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:27,510
Obsessed with these paintings.

210
00:16:27,510 --> 00:16:29,160
Yes, yes.

211
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:31,530
Since you like them,

212
00:16:31,710 --> 00:16:32,510
of course.

213
00:16:38,980 --> 00:16:39,890
Let's go then.

214
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,000
This way.

215
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:03,250
This is our core collection area.

216
00:17:07,069 --> 00:17:08,200
These paintings...

217
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:14,089
Look at this one.

218
00:17:17,869 --> 00:17:20,530
This painting is from
the Southern Qin dynasty.

219
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:23,640
It's the first one I ever collected.

220
00:17:29,930 --> 00:17:32,270
♪ So here is to you ♪

221
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:37,270
♪ My darling ♪

222
00:17:38,250 --> 00:17:45,190
♪ And here is to you, my friend ♪

223
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:53,190
♪ Here is to you, my lover ♪

224
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:50,400
Over there are oil paintings from
the Republic of China era.

225
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:51,000
Come here.

226
00:17:55,230 --> 00:18:01,640
♪ I'll follow you until the end ♪

227
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:00,080
Beautiful, isn't it?

228
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:21,350
♪ So when the fire are burning ♪

229
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:28,720
♪ And when the light fades away ♪

230
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,710
From the Southern Qin
to the Republic of China,

231
00:18:26,710 --> 00:18:28,880
these paintings
cover a huge period of time.

232
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:29,840
And their styles

233
00:18:30,310 --> 00:18:32,310
can be said to vary drastically.

234
00:18:30,590 --> 00:18:37,270
♪ When the sky is falling ♪

235
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,840
I've been criticized
by many people because of this.

236
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,400
They say my art collection

237
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,070
lacks any logic.

238
00:18:39,230 --> 00:18:45,190
♪ I'll never let you be alone ♪

239
00:18:41,310 --> 00:18:42,960
Do you also find it strange?

240
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:46,100
What is my principle
for collecting paintings?

241
00:18:47,990 --> 00:18:49,590
Actually, it's very simple.

242
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:51,230
I just like them.

243
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:04,280
Look at these paintings.

244
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,370
These paintings

245
00:19:08,310 --> 00:19:09,440
have no signatures,

246
00:19:09,990 --> 00:19:11,310
no prominent origins.

247
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:13,880
If put on the art market,

248
00:19:14,470 --> 00:19:16,800
they might even be completely worthless.

249
00:19:22,310 --> 00:19:26,390
♪ So here is to you ♪

250
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:30,150
♪ My darling ♪

251
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:34,030
♪ And here is to you ♪

252
00:19:32,960 --> 00:19:34,680
But whenever I look at them,

253
00:19:34,790 --> 00:19:38,210
♪ My friend ♪

254
00:19:35,030 --> 00:19:35,920
I just feel like

255
00:19:36,750 --> 00:19:38,680
the souls behind these paintings,

256
00:19:38,730 --> 00:19:45,470
♪ Here is to you, my lover ♪

257
00:19:40,230 --> 00:19:42,160
no matter how much time has passed,

258
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:44,240
or how many names they've taken,

259
00:19:45,550 --> 00:19:48,070
seem to be the same person all along.

260
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:55,880
♪ I'll follow you until the end ♪

261
00:19:49,550 --> 00:19:50,510
Someone

262
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:53,400
I love deeply.
